* gm/ID characterization testbench -- sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 (issue #6)
*
* Mirrors nfet_gmid.spice.tmpl's bias/measurement shape for the PFET.
* Source and bulk are tied together at the {VDD} rail (this device's own
* body-tie convention, source-referenced rather than ground-referenced,
* since a PMOS common-source stage in a real circuit is normally biased
* from the top rail). The gate is swept 0 -> VDD exactly like the NFET
* template; bin/sweep.py derives this device's own overdrive axis from the
* swept node directly (Vsg = VDD - v(g)) rather than the sweep direction
* implying it -- see ../README.md's "How to read a record" for the Vov
* definition used here (Vov = Vsg - |Vth|, both read from this same sweep).
* {L}, {W}, {VDRAIN} (the drain bias -- bin/sweep.py sets this to VDD minus
* a representative |Vds|, so the drain sits below the source rail), {VDD},
* {TEMP}, {VSTEP}, {CORNER_INCLUDE} and {OUT_FILE} are substituted by
* bin/sweep.py -- this file itself is never run directly.
*
* Device convention: d/g/s/b = drain/gate/source/bulk. {W} is a
* representative width (see ../README.md); gm/ID, gm/gds and fT are, to
* first order, W-independent normalized quantities.

.option scale=1u
.param mc_mm_switch=0
.param mc_pr_switch=0
.include "{CORNER_INCLUDE}"
.temp {TEMP}

Vg g 0 dc 0
Vsup vdd 0 dc {VDD}
Vdrain d 0 dc {VDRAIN}

XM1 d g vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 l={L} w={W}

.control
save all @m.xm1.msky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8[gm] @m.xm1.msky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8[gds] @m.xm1.msky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8[id] @m.xm1.msky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8[cgg] @m.xm1.msky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8[vth]
dc Vg 0 {VDD} {VSTEP}
wrdata {OUT_FILE} v(g) @m.xm1.msky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8[gm] @m.xm1.msky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8[gds] @m.xm1.msky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8[id] @m.xm1.msky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8[cgg] @m.xm1.msky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8[vth]
.endc
.end
